Installation currently not supported.

To build and run locally, call  "make all"



Legacy Installation instructions:

The library has already been successfully installed on the following
platforms:

- Solaris 2.4 using gcc 2.6.8, tcl 7.3 and tk 3.6 (!!! NO LONGER
                                                       SUPPORTED !!!)

- Solaris 2.5 usgin gcc 2.7.0, tcl 7.4 and tk 4.0
- Solaris 2.5 usgin gcc 2.7.2, tcl 7.5 and tk 4.1
- Linux 1.2.13 using gcc 2.7.0, tcl 7.4 and tk 4.0
- Linux 1.3.80 using gcc 2.7.2, tcl 7.5 and tk 4.1
- Sinix, using the Sinix C++ compiler and the motif widget set (although I
  have never seen this one myself )

To install the library you need the following Programs and libraries
installed on your system:

- g++ version 2.6.3 or higher.
- libg++ according to the compiler.
- X11R5 or higher
- tcl 7.4 and tk 4.0 (recommended)
or
- tcl 7.3 and tk 3.6 optional with the tkPixmap
  extension. (!!! NO LONGER SUPPORTED !!!)

If you want to compile the .y and .l files you need (Precompiled .cc
and .h files are included in the distribution) :

- bison++ 1.21-8 
- flex++ 2.3.8-7 (the real flex++, not the one from the flex distribution !!!) 

If you want to change some of the configure files you also need:

- autoconf
- autoheader

If you want to be able to use Xpm images you also need the

- Xpm library (recommended)

To install the library do the following:

- You might want to edit the top section of 
  "./include/ffgraph/ffGlobdefs.h.in"

- Type "./configure". You may want to pass some options
  like "--prefix=/usr/local" to configure.

- make dependall (optional, but recommended)
- make
- make install
- make install.lib
- make cleanall (if you want to save disc-space)
- If all worked fine, stand up and pat yourself on the
  shoulder

TROUBLESHOUTING:

If something went wrong, maybe one of the following could help:


- Error: " make: Warning: Can't find `Makefile.dependencies'"

  Solution:

  Somehow a dependencies file got lost. This can happen if you
  interrupt "make" at a wrong moment. Go to the corresponding
  directory and type "touch Makefile.dependencies".

- Error: "gcc: tk.h: No such file or directory"

  Solution:

  The tcl/tk header files are not where the library expects them. Add
  the directory to "INCLUDES" in "Makefile.head.common.in" and
  rerun "configure".

- Error: tkAppInit.c: tcl_RcFileName unkown variable

  Solution:
  
  comment out the line 
  tcl_RcFileName = "~/.wishrc";

- Error: "ld: fatal: library -lxxx: not found"

  Solution:

  The library xxx ist not where the ffgraph library expected it. Add
  the apropriat directory to "LDFLAGS" in "Makefile.head.common.in'
  and rerun "configure".

- Error: Any other error

  Solution:

  - Find the error, fix it and send a patch to "friedric@fmi.uni-passau.de"

  - Send a bug report to "friedric@fmi.uni-passau.de" containing:

    - Kind of computer you use
    - Kind and version of operating system you use
    - Kind and version of compiler you use
    - Version of ffgraph library you use
    - Detailed description of the error, including a description on
      how to reproduce it.
